    "result_text": "Tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI updated the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` in `AssignCustomerCode.java`:\n\n- **CITY3** \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the owner's city\n- **LAST3** \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the lastName (unchanged)\n- **NNNN** \u2014 now a **per-city** 4-digit sequence: one more than the number of owners already in that city (previously a global count), computed by filtering `findAll()` on matching city\n\n**Derived values rebuilt automatically:** the membership number in `OwnerMapper` is built as `owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + <year>`. Because it concatenates the full `customerCode` string, it now carries the new `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` prefix without needing a code change \u2014 e.g. `LON-SMI-0007-M26`.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserting the `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` shape) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0).",
