    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is localized, additive, and idiomatic:\n\n- The new CITY3 logic mirrors the existing LAST3 logic exactly (same `substring(0, Math.min(3, \u2026)).toUpperCase()` idiom), so it reads as a natural extension rather than a bolt-on.\n- The per-city sequence is a clean refactor of the prior global count (`findAll().size() + 1` \u2192 a filtered stream `.count() + 1`), keeping the counting logic in the same unit where it already lived. No new class or helper is warranted for this.\n- The Javadoc was updated in step with the code, and its description stays accurate to the new behavior.\n- The one derived value, `membershipNumber` in `OwnerMapper` (`owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + \u2026`), composes on the **whole** customerCode string and never parses its internal structure, so it rebuilds on the new format automatically \u2014 no duplicated format knowledge to keep in sync, and nothing structurally left stale. No other code reads or parses `customerCode`.\n\nLogic is in the right unit, nothing is duplicated, and `AssignCustomerCode` remains a single-responsibility step consistent with the project's function-per-step convention.",
